# Plan Creation Instructions

These instructions are read by the plan writer agent every time it creates
a new execution plan. Use this file to encode project-specific conventions,
constraints, and domain knowledge that every plan should respect.

## Architecture constraints

- All shell scripts must pass `shellcheck` and `shfmt`
- Core artifacts (scripts/, hooks/, commands/) must remain project-agnostic
- Domain-specific logic goes in `canon/`, never in core

## Plan style

- Progress log items should be small enough for one agent session (~15 min)
- Prefer sequential plans unless items are truly independent
- Every plan must have verifiable completion criteria (commands, not prose)
- Include "Files to touch" table so reviewers can assess blast radius

## What to avoid

- No UI work of any kind
- No changes to CI/CD pipelines without explicit approval
- No new dependencies without justification in the decision log

## Domain knowledge

- The orchestrator runs in tmux with one pane per worker
- Workers operate in isolated git worktrees
- Plans are committed before the orchestrator runs them
- dega-core.yaml at repo root configures per-project settings
